@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ Exa is a Web Search API. Add Exa web search to your LLMs in a few lines of code.
 npm install @exalabs/ai-sdk
 ```
 
+Works with AI SDK 6 and 7 (`ai@^6 || ^7`) and with zod 3.25+ or zod 4.
+
 ## Quick Start
 
 ```typescript
@@ -46,7 +48,7 @@ Get your API key from the [Exa Dashboard](https://dashboard.exa.ai/api-keys).
 - Type: `auto` (best search)
 - Results: `10`
 - Text: `3000 characters per result`
-- Livecrawl: `fallback` for backwards compatibility. Prefer `contents.maxAgeHours` when you need explicit freshness.
+- Freshness: the API default (cached content when available, live crawl otherwise). Set `contents.maxAgeHours` when you need explicit freshness.
 
 ## Setup
 
@@ -203,6 +205,17 @@ webSearch({
 })
 ```
 
+## Cancellation and errors
+
+The tool forwards the AI SDK's `abortSignal` to its request, so stopping a
+`generateText` / `streamText` call (or passing `AbortSignal.timeout(ms)`) also
+cancels the Exa request. Non-2xx responses throw an `ExaApiError` with
+`status`, `tag` (for example `INVALID_API_KEY`, `RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`),
+`requestId`, and `retryAfterSeconds` when Exa sends `Retry-After`.
+
+Pass `fetch` in the config to route requests through your own fetch
+implementation.
+
 ## TypeScript Support
 
 Full TypeScript types included, including typed structured output:
